    "title": "Darkness Level Equals Provable Witness Cardinality",
    "description": "In a sound proof system with an existential and an 'at least k witnesses' operator, define the darkness level of a one-place predicate T as the supremum of k for which the system proves 'there are at least k witnesses of T' while proving no individual instance T(n). Conjecture that this supremum is a well-defined ordinal invariant, that it is monotone under sound interpretations between systems, and that a predicate is dark of level exactly k precisely when the system's provable lower bound on the true witness set is k. Approach: extend the finite Finset drop-one monotonicity argument to a transfinite counting operator indexed by ordinals, and prove an exactness theorem separating level k from level k+1 by exhibiting, for each k, a model whose true-atom set has cardinality exactly k. Test the invariant on layered models where atoms become true along a prescribed filtration.",
